<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reuss (river)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Reuss is a river in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, about 160 kilometres long. Rising near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotthard-pass">Gotthard Pass</a>, it flows through the canton of Uri and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schollenen-gorge">Schöllenen</a> gorge into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-lucerne">Lake Lucerne</a>, leaves the lake at the city of Lucerne and joins the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aare">Aare</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brugg">Brugg</a>. Its valley carried the Gotthard route that made Uri and Lucerne important from the 13th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reuss-river.jpg" alt="Reuss (river)" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edwin Lee · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kapellbrucke_in_Lucerne.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
